ine":640,"endColumn":39,"suggestions":"26615","suppressions":"26616"},{"ruleId":"26548","severity":1,"message":"26549","line":45,"column":7,"nodeType":"26550","messageId":"26551","endLine":45,"endColumn":38},{"ruleId":"26552","severity":1,"message":"26617","line":680,"column":5,"nodeType":"26554","endLine":680,"endColumn":39,"suggestions":"26618"},{"ruleId":"26559","severity":1,"message":"26560","line":28,"column":7,"nodeType":"26561","endLine":28,"endColumn":63,"suppressions":"26619"},{"ruleId":"26559","severity":1,"message":"26560","line":43,"column":9,"nodeType":"26561","endLine":43,"endColumn":64,"suppressions":"26620"},{"ruleId":"26548","severity":1,"message":"26621","line":521,"column":3,"nodeType":"26622","messageId":"26551","endLine":521,"endColumn":86},"@next/next/no-location-assign-relative-destination","Do not use `window.location.href` to navigate to internal Next.js pages. Use `redirect()` in the render phase, or `useRouter().push()` in Client Components' event handlers instead. See: https://nextjs.org/docs/messages/no-location-assign-relative-destination","AssignmentExpression","noLocationAssign","react-hooks/exhaustive-deps","React Hook useMemo has a missing dependency: 'locale'. Either include it or remove the dependency array.","ArrayExpression",["26623"],"React Hook useEffect has a missing dependency: 't'. Either include it or remove the dependency array.",["26624"],["26625"],"@next/next/no-img-element","Using `<img>` could result in slower LCP and higher bandwidth. Consider using `<Image />` from `next/image` or a custom image loader to automatically optimize images. This may incur additional usage or cost from your provider. See: https://nextjs.org/docs/messages/no-img-element","JSXOpeningElement",["26626"],["26627"],"React Hook useLayoutEffect contains a call to 'setSingle'. Without a list of dependencies, this can lead to an infinite chain of updates. To fix this, pass [] as a second argument to the useLayoutEffect Hook.","MemberExpression",["26628"],["26629"],"React Hook useEffect has missing dependencies: 'onStateChange' and 'state'. Either include them or remove the dependency array. If 'onStateChange' changes too often, find the parent component that defines it and wrap that definition in useCallback.",["26630"],["26631"],"@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars","'showIcon' is assigned a value but never used. Allowed unused args must match /^_/u.","Identifier","unusedVar","'stats' is assigned a value but never used. Allowed unused vars must match /^_/u.",["26632"],"React Hook useMemo has an unnecessary dependency: 'key'. Either exclude it or remove the dependency array.",["26633"],["26634"],["26635"],["26636"],"React Hook useCallback has a missing dependency: 't'. Either include it or remove the dependency array.",["26637"],["26638"],"React Hook useEffect has missing dependencies: 'q', 'setPage', and 'setQ'. Either include them or remove the dependency array.",["26639"],["26640"],"'dfLocale' is assigned a value but never used. Allowed unused vars must match /^_/u.","React Hook useEffect has a missing dependency: 'initialValue'. Either include it or remove the dependency array. If 'setPreviewed' needs the current value of 'initialValue', you can also switch to useReducer instead of useState and read 'initialValue' in the reducer.",["26641"],["26642"],"React Hook useEffect has missing dependencies: 'initialKey' and 'initialValue'. Either include them or remove the dependency array. If 'setPreviewed' needs the current value of 'initialValue', you can also switch to useReducer instead of useState and read 'initialValue' in the reducer.",["26643"],["26644"],"React Hook useEffect has missing dependencies: 'ids', 'onResults', and 'status'. Either include them or remove the dependency array. If 'onResults' changes too often, find the parent component that defines it and wrap that definition in useCallback.",["26645"],["26646"],["26647"],"React Hook useEffect has missing dependencies: 'findings', 'n', and 't'. Either include them or remove the dependency array. If 'setTitle' needs the current value of 'findings', you can also switch to useReducer instead of useState and read 'findings' in the reducer.",["26648"],["26649"],"React Hook useEffect has missing dependencies: 'initialQuery' and 'initialTitle'. Either include them or remove the dependency array. If 'setQuery' needs the current value of 'initialQuery', you can also switch to useReducer instead of useState and read 'initialQuery' in the reducer.",["26650"],["26651"],"React Hook useEffect has a missing dependency: 'choose'. Either include it or remove the dependency array.",["26652"],["26653"],"React Hook useEffect has a missing dependency: 'initialRanges'. Either include it or remove the dependency array. If 'setRangesText' needs the current value of 'initialRanges', you can also switch to useReducer instead of useState and read 'initialRanges' in the reducer.",["26654"],["26655"],"React Hook useEffect has missing dependencies: 'onChange' and 'schedule'. Either include them or remove the dependency array. If 'onChange' changes too often, find the parent component that defines it and wrap that definition in useCallback.",["26656"],["26657"],"React Hook React.useMemo has a missing dependency: 't'. Either include it or remove the dependency array.",["26658"],["26659"],"React Hook useMemo has an unnecessary dependency: 'dateLocale'. Either exclude it or remove the dependency array.",["26660"],["26661"],["26662"],"Do not use `window.location.assign()` to navigate to internal Next.js pages. Use `redirect()` in the render phase, or `useRouter().push()` in Client Components' event handlers instead. See: https://nextjs.org/docs/messages/no-location-assign-relative-destination","CallExpression",{"desc":"26663","fix":"26664"},{"desc":"26665","fix":"26666"},{"kind":"26667","justification":"26668"},{"kind":"26667","justification":"26669"},{"kind":"26667","justification":"26669"},{"desc":"26670","fix":"26671"},{"kind":"26667","justi